ROOT CAUSE (pre-existing, repo-wide, NOT this surface):
  Several sibling dashboard-widget surfaces declare Swift types whose bare names (ChargeSessionDTO,
  ChargeStatusUpdate, ChargeDistanceUnit, …) collide with same-named types exported by the imported KMP
  `Shared.xcframework` (ADR-004), so the whole-module app build fails with "ambiguous for type lookup"
  on those siblings — on BOTH platforms — independent of this surface (0 DriveHighlightSlide diagnostics in
  every build/typecheck above). On macOS the build additionally needs a development signing certificate that
  this CI-less host lacks. BOTH conditions live OUTSIDE this prompt's allowed scope (DriveHighlightSlide.*
  only): fixing the collisions means renaming/module-qualifying sibling widget types, and enabling signing
  means editing apps/apple/project.yml — each parallel-unsafe to touch from a single surface slot (Honesty
  Covenant #7 "No predecessor bypass"). This matches the established precedent for every P4 feature-view
  surface (e.g. 0063 EnvironmentSlide, 0005, 0086): the signed Xcode app build/test is DEFERRED to the
  integration runner; the surface is verified via host gates + both-SDK SDK compiles + executed
  projection/model tests. THIS surface deliberately prefixes ALL of its types (DriveHighlightReviewDTO,
  DriveHighlightSlideUpdate, DriveHighlightSlideDistanceUnit, …) so it does NOT collide and contributes 0
  errors. Evidence captured (not assumed) in /tmp/dhs_harness/{ios_build,ios_buildtest,mac_buildtest,
  mac_build_nosign,xcframework,harness}.log.

